label("$D$",(5,0),E);[/asy]

Dots are spaced one unit part, horizontally and vertically. What is the number of square units enclosed by the polygon?
[asy]
/* AMC8 1998 #6P */
size(1inch,1inch);
pair a=(0,0), b=(10,0), c=(20,0), d=(30, 0);
pair e=(0,10), f=(10,10), g=(20,10), h=(30,10);
pair i=(0,20), j=(10,20), k=(20,20), l=(30,20);
pair m=(0,30), n=(10,30), o=(20,30), p=(30,30);
dot(a);
dot(b);
dot(c);
dot(d);
dot(e);
dot(f);
dot(g);
dot(h);
dot(i);
dot(j);
dot(k);
dot(l);
dot(m);
dot(n);
dot(o);
dot(p);
draw(a--b--g--c--d--h--l--k--o--j--i--e--a);
[/asy]

A circular dartboard is divided into regions with various central angles, as shown. The probability of a dart randomly landing in a particular region is $\frac16$. What is the corresponding measure, in degrees, of the central angle of this section of the dartboard? [asy]
unitsize(1.5cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt));

pair O=(0,0);
draw(Circle(O,1));
draw(dir(0)--O--dir(90));
draw(dir(150)--O--dir(225));
[/asy]

What is the ratio of the area of triangle $BDC$ to the area of triangle $ADC$? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(10sqrt(3),0)--(0,10)--(0,0)--cycle,linewidth(2));
draw(5sqrt(3)*dir(60)--(0,0),linewidth(2));

draw((1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1),linewidth(1));
draw(5sqrt(3)*dir(60)+1*dir(-120)--(5sqrt(3)-1)*dir(60)+1*dir(-30)--5sqrt(3)*dir(60)+1*dir(-30),linewidth(1));

label("A",(10sqrt(3),0),E);
label("B",(0,10),W);
label("C",(0,0),SW);
label("D",5sqrt(3)*dir(60),NE);
label("$30^{\circ}$",(12,0),N);
[/asy]
